### 2. Fix the NullPointerException in Batch Counting (C-7)
If a batch doesn't exist, queryForObject returns null, which crashes when Java tries to convert it to a primitive long.
**File:** JournalRequestServiceImpl.java
**Method:** getRequestCountByBatchId()
**Replace the entire method with this:**
```java
    @Override
    public long getRequestCountByBatchId(String batchId) {
        try {
            Long result = jdbcTemplate.queryForObject(
                "SELECT NVL(TOTAL_ROWS, 0) FROM JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER WHERE BATCH_ID = ?", Long.class, batchId);
            return result != null ? result : 0L;
        } catch (EmptyResultDataAccessException e) {
            log.warn("COUNT_NOT_FOUND | Batch: {} | Status: Batch not in master table", batchId);
            return 0L;
        } catch (DataAccessException e) {
            log.error("COUNT_QUERY_FAIL | Batch: {} | Status: Query failure", batchId);
            return 0L;
        }
    }

```
### 3. Secure the cancelMyRequest Endpoint (H-6)
Right now, any logged-in user can delete any other user's journal requests if they know the ID. We must enforce an ownership check.
**File:** JournalRequestServiceImpl.java
**Method:** cancelMyRequest()
**Replace the entire method with this:**
```java
    @Override
    @Transactional
    public void cancelMyRequest(Long requestId, String userId) {
        JournalRequest request = journalRequestRepository.findById(requestId)
            .orElseThrow(() -> new RuntimeException("Request not found: " + requestId)); // Replace RuntimeException with your custom ResourceNotFoundException if you have one

        // CRITICAL FIX: Security Ownership Check
        if (!request.getCreatorId().equalsIgnoreCase(userId)) {
            log.warn("UNAUTHORIZED_DELETE | User: {} | RequestOwner: {} | ReqID: {}", userId, request.getCreatorId(), requestId);
            throw new IllegalStateException("You can only cancel your own requests.");
        }

        if (request.getRequestStatus() != RequestStatus.PENDING) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Only PENDING requests can be cancelled. Current: " + request.getRequestStatus());
        }

        journalRequestRepository.delete(request);
        log.info("REQUEST_CANCELLED | User: {} | ReqID: {}", userId, requestId);
    }

```
### 4. Fix Inconsistent Pagination (NH-2)
